      "message" : "`GET /contracts/{id}` should now return an `audit` object with `createdBy`, `createdAt`, `lastModifiedBy` and `lastModifiedAt`. I confirmed that the build passes and that the generated response includes `audit`. I did not exercise the endpoint, since the project has no tests, so the timestamps and user names are untested.\n\n- **`Contract.java`:** I added an `AuditInfo audit` component, which Prefab fills in on create and update. It is not part of any request record, so clients can't set it. `createdBy`/`createdAt` are written only on creation. `lastModifiedBy`/`lastModifiedAt` are written on creation and on every `PUT /contracts/{id}`.\n- **`SecurityAuditContextProvider.java` (new):** this supplies the user as the Spring Security principal name. It falls back to `\"system\"` when nobody is authenticated.\n- **Migration:** the generated `V1__generated.sql` already includes the four `audit_*` columns. It is written to `target/classes/db/migration/` at build time, and Prefab's docs recommend copying it into `src/main/resources/db/migration/` to keep it in source control."
