      "message" : "The `/documents` upload and download endpoints are in place, and `mvn clean test` passes.\n\n`Document` in `com.example.documents` has a `title` and a `file`, with `@GetById`, `@Create` and `@Download` on it. That gives you `POST /documents` (multipart with a JSON `body` part and a `file` part, responding `201` with a `Location` header), `GET /documents/{id}` and `GET /documents/{id}/file`.\n\nThe `@ContentType` and `@FileSize` annotations had no effect in this Prefab version, because the processor doesn't copy them into the generated request record. Uploads of any type or size were returning `201`. So the `Document` constructor now checks the file itself and throws `BadRequestException`, which returns `400`. It accepts only `application/pdf` and `image/png`, up to 1,048,576 bytes. I left the annotations on the aggregate as documentation.\n\nThe new `DocumentIntegrationTest` covers three things:\n- **Upload and download:** a PDF round-trips with its original bytes and content type, and `GET /documents/{id}` returns the title.\n- **Rejected uploads:** `text/plain` and a 1,048,577-byte PNG both get `400`.\n- **Size limit:** a PNG of exactly 1,048,576 bytes is accepted.\n\nThe test output shows two ERROR log lines from the rejected uploads, which are expected."
    },
